## FPGA Implementation Results

**Target FPGA:** AMD Zynq UltraScale+ ZU3EG (`xczu3eg-sfvc784-2-e`)  
**Development Tool:** AMD Xilinx Vivado 2024.2.2  
**Implementation Status:** Routed

### Resource Utilization

| Resource | Used | Utilization |
|---|---:|---:|
| CLB LUTs | 20 | 0.03% |
| Flip-flops | 37 | 0.03% |
| CLBs | 6 | 0.07% |
| BRAM tiles | 0 | 0% |
| DSP slices | 0 | 0% |
| CARRY8 | 0 | 0% |
| BUFGCE | 1 | 1.14% |

### Timing Analysis

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Primary clock target | 100 MHz |
| Clock period | 10 ns |
| Clock uncertainty | 0.2 ns |
| Worst Negative Slack (WNS) | +7.431 ns |
| Total Negative Slack (TNS) | 0 ns |
| Worst Hold Slack (WHS) | +0.021 ns |
| Total Hold Slack (THS) | 0 ns |
| Failing setup endpoints | 0 |
| Failing hold endpoints | 0 |

### Timing Analysis Methodology

1. Defined a 100 MHz primary system clock using an XDC constraint.
2. Applied 0.2 ns clock uncertainty.
3. Performed RTL simulation using Vivado.
4. Executed synthesis, placement and routing.
5. Evaluated setup and hold timing using Vivado Static Timing Analysis.
6. Analysed FPGA resource utilization using the Vivado utilization report.

*Timing results are based on the specified primary system clock constraint. External SPI interface delays and generated-clock constraints are not included in the current XDC.*

